Docker build with (amd64 — the pinned pandas/numpy only have musllinux wheels
for x86_64; an arm64 build compiles them from source):

docker image build \
--platform linux/amd64 \
--tag kg:test \
.

Docker run with (the listener reads /kg/.env.local when present; in k8s the
same variables come from the secret/configmap instead):

docker run --rm -it \
--env-file=.env.local.dockerized \
--mount type=bind,source=.env.local.dockerized,target=/kg/.env.local,readonly \
--network=host \
kg:test

Offline smoke test without RabbitMQ (same image, one fixture document):

docker run --rm -it \
--env-file=.env.local.dockerized \
--network=host \
--mount type=bind,source=./data,target=/kg/data,readonly \
kg:test --once data/<dir>/<doc>.json
